        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "Pessimistic",
            "Optimistic"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "High contention",
              "**wins**",
              "retry storm"
            ],
            [
              "Rare conflict",
              "wasted waits",
              "**wins**"
            ],
            [
              "Lock hold",
              "read→commit",
              "write only"
            ],
            [
              "Deadlock risk",
              "real",
              "near zero"
            ],
            [
              "Reader impact",
              "blocks FOR UPDATE",
              "none"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. ORM traps",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hibernate `@Version`: adds `AND version=?`, throws on 0 rows",
            "Django `select_for_update()`: real `FOR UPDATE`, needs `atomic()`",
            "Rails `with_lock`: opens transaction **and** `lock!` reloads row",
            "`optimistic_locking` silently no-ops without a version column"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Locks outside the row model",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`pg_advisory_xact_lock(key)`: auto-released at COMMIT",
            "`GET_LOCK('job',10)` in MySQL: session-scoped, **survives** rollback",
            "Use for cron singletons, no row to lock on",
            "Hash a string key to bigint; collisions are silent"
          ],
          "style": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Last resort: idempotency",
          "items": [
            "Client sends `Idempotency-Key` header",
            "`UNIQUE(idempotency_key)` on the table",
            "Duplicate INSERT fails 23505 → return stored result",
            "Only the constraint truly stops the retry"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Pick one, then commit to it",
          "text": "Pessimistic buys you blocking and deadlocks; optimistic buys you a __retry loop you must actually write__. CAS beats both when the whole update fits one statement."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Two Quirks That Bite",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "-- MySQL RR, snapshot at T0",
            "SELECT bal FROM acct WHERE id=1;",
            "-- 100 (snapshot)",
            "SELECT bal FROM acct WHERE id=1",
            "  FOR UPDATE;  -- 250 (latest!)"
          ],
          "note": "locking reads skip the snapshot"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "postgresql",
      "subtitle": "Two ways to win a race"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Engine Differences & Trade-offs",
      "blocks": [
        {
