    {
      "page_title": "Measuring Contention & the Lost Update",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Benchmark rule",
          "text": "Plot **abort/retry rate** beside throughput. Retries hide as ==latency, not errors== — a green error dashboard with p99 climbing is a serialization problem."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Connection pools leak state",
          "items": [
            "Borrower left mid-txn returns the conn __dirty__.",
            "Next borrower inherits its locks + `SET TRANSACTION` level.",
            "Symptom: random isolation, ghost blockers on idle apps.",
            "Fix: `ROLLBACK` on release; reset session vars."
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Replicas Are Not Isolation",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Read replica = a cheap ==consistent snapshot== for reports.",
            "Price: __replication lag__ — you read the past, not a level.",
            "Write-then-read on a replica returns the pre-write row.",
            "Never route a read-modify-write through a replica."
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Measure, Don't Guess",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
